{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Cub6neWd9Hf7yY3aJq7W6e", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asmat_people\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asmat_Regency\"}, {\"url\": \"https://p2k.stekom.ac.id/ensiklopedia/Fumeripits\"}, {\"url\": \"https://e-journal.usd.ac.id/index.php/Divinitas/article/download/7499/pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://m.guardian.ng/life/asmat-the-tribe-where-cannibalism-makes-you-a-real-man/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.dspace.cam.ac.uk/handle/1810/338162\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.everyculture.com/Oceania/Asmat-Orientation.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ejurnal.ung.ac.id/index.php/jhcj/article/download/26520/9043\"}, {\"url\": \"https://wikipedia.com/wiki/Asmat_tribe\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:09:14.131Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Suku Asmat tiga konsep dunia Amat ow Capinmi Dampu ow Campinmi Safar", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01SVh3tfvsYpqY5Gv5fYvWBH", "content": [{"title": "Asmat people", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asmat_people"}, {"title": "Asmat Regency", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asmat_Regency"}, {"title": "p2k.stekom.ac.id", "url": "https://p2k.stekom.ac.id/ensiklopedia/Fumeripits"}, {"title": "e-journal.usd.ac.id", "url": "https://e-journal.usd.ac.id/index.php/Divinitas/article/download/7499/pdf"}, {"title": "Asmat: The Tribe Where Cannibalism Makes You A Real Man", "url": "https://m.guardian.ng/life/asmat-the-tribe-where-cannibalism-makes-you-a-real-man/"}, {"title": "The three hearths: Custom, church and state as colliding orders of time and space in Asmat, Indonesian Papua", "url": "https://www.dspace.cam.ac.uk/handle/1810/338162"}, {"title": "Asmat Orientation", "url": "https://www.everyculture.com/Oceania/Asmat-Orientation.html"}, {"title": "ung.ac.id", "url": "https://ejurnal.ung.ac.id/index.php/jhcj/article/download/26520/9043"}, {"title": "Asmat people", "url": "https://wikipedia.com/wiki/Asmat_tribe"}]}, "The search found one directly relevant source, a 2024 Indonesian journal article on Fumeripits, which describes the three-world concept. The spellings in the source differ from your query. It uses \"Asamat Ow Capinmi,\" \"Damir Ow Capinmi,\" and \"Safan\" where you wrote \"Amat ow,\" \"Capinmi Dampu ow,\" and \"Campinmi Safar.\"\n\n- **The three worlds:** The article says the Asmat hold to three realms: the world of the living, a stopover place, and Safan, which it identifies as heaven. The Asmat people believe that their ancestor was a young man who was skilled in the art of carving. They believe there are three worlds, namely Asamat Ow Capinmi (world of the living), Damir Ow Capinmi (stopover place), and Safan (Heaven).\n- **Moral duty in the living world:** The same source links life in the first realm to duties. In Asamat Ow Capinmi, the Asmat community has an obligation to do good and obey customary law.\n- **Role of the stopover realm:** The article ties the stopover world to ancestors. Its fragment says the community acts to help ancestors experience liberation from Damir Ow Capinmi.\n- **Fumeripits:** The article presents Fumeripits as the highest god, above the ancestors, and the creator. Fumeripits is seen as the highest god, above the ancestors of the Asmat tribe, who is considered the creator, having higher power and authority. The journal is a DOI-registered article (10.24071/div.v2i1.7499) in Divinitas.\n- **Background:** A general encyclopedia entry says the Asmat refer to their home area as Asmat capinmi, the Asmat world. That supports the \"capinmi\" term as meaning \"world\" in this context.\n\nNo source in these results confirms the exact spellings \"Capinmi Dampu ow\" or \"Campinmi Safar,\" or gives more detail on the stopover realm beyond the single article. Further searches in Indonesian or on Asmat cosmology would be needed to verify the spelling and details."], "durationSeconds": 6.788948707999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Cub6neWd9Hf7yY3aJq7W6e", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
